    <string name="tip_net_worth">Wallet + buy-order escrow + items (assets at Jita sell + items listed in sell orders). Change is over the selected range. Escrow history is rebuilt from the wallet journal; items are recorded once a day from the dashboard\'s first run, before that they\'re estimated as stock at FIFO cost plus the difference seen on that first day.</string>
    <string name="items">Items</string>
    <string name="in_sell_orders">%1$s in sell orders</string>
    <string name="tip_items">Everything you own besides ISK: assets from the background refresh, valued at Jita sell, plus items listed in sell orders (listed items leave the asset list) at their order price.</string>
    <string name="tip_escrow">ISK reserved by open buy orders (price × remaining). Skills can lower the real escrow, so this is the upper bound.</string>
    <string name="tip_stock">Unsold items at what they cost you (FIFO, including the buy broker fee) — includes items listed in sell orders.</string>
    <string name="tip_stock_market">The same stock at the lowest Jita 4-4 sell, after sales tax and broker fee; below it, the unrealized profit.</string>
    <string name="tip_cash_flow">ISK actually in and out of the wallet over the range: sales minus purchases, taxes and fees. Buying stock shows as a loss here even if you'll sell it at a profit later.</string>
    <string name="tip_realized_pnl">Profit on what you actually sold over the range: sale price minus what those same units cost you (FIFO — first bought, first sold), after fees. Unsold stock doesn\'t count.</string>
